WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.630 --> 00:00:07.290
There is a conservative, a British politician
who rung a green peace activists neck when

00:00:07.290 --> 00:00:10.130
she interrupted a speech in the United Kingdom
a few days ago.

00:00:10.130 --> 00:00:12.140
And I'm going to set this up for you.

00:00:12.140 --> 00:00:17.480
Mark Field is a member of parliament or an
MP as they are known in the United Kingdom.

00:00:17.480 --> 00:00:18.920
He's 54 years old.

00:00:18.920 --> 00:00:24.119
He's a member of the Conservative Party in
the UK, also known as the Tories and a few

00:00:24.119 --> 00:00:29.119
days ago, Chancellor Philip Hammond was giving
a speech about Brexit at what's called the

00:00:29.119 --> 00:00:32.059
bankers and merchants dinner.

00:00:32.059 --> 00:00:36.090
Greenpeace Greenpeace is the climate activist
organization.

00:00:36.090 --> 00:00:41.870
They sent 40 volunteers to do, uh, to this
event to try to interfere with the speech

00:00:41.870 --> 00:00:44.340
and get attention for climate change.

00:00:44.340 --> 00:00:49.830
One woman was walking around there as part
of this protest and Mark Fields got up and

00:00:49.830 --> 00:00:54.060
grabbed her and pushed her and then rung her
neck.

00:00:54.060 --> 00:00:57.660
Some might almost call it strangling from
behind, although I don't know that that's

00:00:57.660 --> 00:01:00.010
the right term in this particular case.

00:01:00.010 --> 00:01:01.010
And there is video.

00:01:01.010 --> 00:01:06.659
So immediately the question is, is this treatment
too rough for someone that seems to be one

00:01:06.659 --> 00:01:08.100
of 40 peaceful protesters.

00:01:08.100 --> 00:01:10.439
Some have argued she could have had a gun.

00:01:10.439 --> 00:01:14.259
Hard to imagine from the dress she was wearing
that she had a gun.

00:01:14.259 --> 00:01:19.009
Not to mention both of her hands were full
of items, which would make it quite difficult

00:01:19.009 --> 00:01:22.329
to even get a gun out of her purse if that's
what she had.

00:01:22.329 --> 00:01:23.810
And where she had it.

00:01:23.810 --> 00:01:29.939
Fields is saying his reaction was quite instinctive
given the circumstances and fields has since

00:01:29.939 --> 00:01:31.619
apologized to the woman.

00:01:31.619 --> 00:01:34.500
There are other mps calling for this guy to
go.

00:01:34.500 --> 00:01:39.639
Labour, MP, Tanya Antone, artsy says quote,
no one who reacts like this to a peaceful

00:01:39.639 --> 00:01:41.999
protest should be sitting in our parliament.

00:01:41.999 --> 00:01:48.180
Liberal Democrat, MP Chuka Umunna, uh, says
that the actions are totally unacceptable.

00:01:48.180 --> 00:01:52.670
Former Tory MP, Sarah Wallace and says, it
was quote absolutely shameful.

00:01:52.670 --> 00:01:58.170
A male MP marching a woman out of a room by
her neck, Labor Minister Don Butler tweeted,

00:01:58.170 --> 00:01:59.179
this is horrific.

00:01:59.179 --> 00:02:01.950
Mark field must immediately be suspended or
sacked.

00:02:01.950 --> 00:02:08.569
Bottom line, a woman in a ball gown with high
heels holding a cell phone and a small purse

00:02:08.569 --> 00:02:14.080
is not the threat that instinctively was apparently
what went to Mark Fields.

00:02:14.080 --> 00:02:16.220
Mind here, it's extremely difficult to buy
that.

00:02:16.220 --> 00:02:21.380
Now, some people are making this a man versus
woman issue saying, Oh, you're only upset

00:02:21.380 --> 00:02:25.780
because the protester was a woman, but it
would've been totally fine if the protest

00:02:25.780 --> 00:02:26.780
or had been a man.

00:02:26.780 --> 00:02:29.470
There is no question that gender is a factor
here.

00:02:29.470 --> 00:02:35.170
I would argue it's a reasonable factor, but
beyond that, a sitting MP, putting his hands

00:02:35.170 --> 00:02:39.570
on a member of the public's throat is now
what we're defending.

00:02:39.570 --> 00:02:44.390
I got an email from a viewer saying the way
this guy reacted, his entire posture, his

00:02:44.390 --> 00:02:49.200
entire demeanor during this is of a classic
domestic abuser.

00:02:49.200 --> 00:02:56.230
I would not argue that this guy is a domestic
abuser, absent evidence that he is a domestic

00:02:56.230 --> 00:02:57.750
of view abuser.

00:02:57.750 --> 00:03:02.050
What I do believe is that this is a level
of aggression that did come naturally to me,

00:03:02.050 --> 00:03:08.110
to to him in the moment, and I can also tell
you that in the United States, far less aggressive

00:03:08.110 --> 00:03:13.010
physical attacks than this often lead to people
being charged with battery.

00:03:13.010 --> 00:03:14.410
So I want to hear from you.

00:03:14.410 --> 00:03:15.410
What do you think about this?

00:03:15.410 --> 00:03:19.800
If you've been listening to the podcast or
radio show and you, you didn't see the video

00:03:19.800 --> 00:03:24.203
that we just played for a video audience,
find the video online and let me know what

00:03:24.203 --> 00:03:24.212
you think of it.

